hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1593","On the authority of Muhammad bin Bashar, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Hisham bin Abi Abdullah, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Yunus bin Jubayr, on the authority of Hattan bin Abdullah. H. Bundar told us, Ibn Abi Adi told us. H, Harun bin Ishaq Al-Hamdani narrated to us, Abdah narrated to us, both of them on the authority of Saeed bin Abi Orouba, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Yunus bin Jubayr, on the authority of Hattan bin Abdullah Al-Raqqashi, and this is the hadith of Abdah, he said: Abu Musa Al-Ash’ari led us in prayer, and when he sat at the end of his prayer, he said One of them said: Prayer was established with righteousness and zakat, and when Abu Musa Al-Ash’ari turned away, he said: Which of you says such-and-such a word? Do you not know what to say in your prayers? The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, addressed us, explained to us our Sunnah, and taught us our prayers. He said: “When you pray, straighten your rows. And let one of you lead you in prayer. When the imam says “Allahu Akbar,” say “Allahu Akbar,” and when he says: “Not with anger upon them, nor with those who go astray,” then say: “Amen, God loves you,” and when He said “Allahu Akbar” and bowed, so “Allahu Akbar” and bowed, for the Imam bows before you and rises before you.” The Prophet of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “So that is Thus, when he says takbeer and prostrates, then prostrate, for the imam prostrates before you, and rises before you.” Bundar added: Then the Prophet of God said: “So that’s the same.” Abu Bakr said: He means that the imam precedes you in bowing, so he kneels before you, so you raise your heads from bowing after he raises. So you remain in the bowing, and this staying in the bowing after the imam raises the head from the bowing is the precedence with which the imam preceded you in bowing. The same applies to prostration"
